  "standard": "732.1-B-3 §4.1, §4.3.11.3.4 — frames of channels the configuration does not hold",
  "provenance": "hand-derived",
  "provenance_note": "Hand-derived from 732.1-B-3 §4.1.2 (Primary Header: TFVN 1100 bits 0-3, SCID bits 4-19, Source-or-Destination bit 20, VCID bits 21-26, MAP ID bits 27-30, End of Frame Primary Header Flag bit 31, Frame Length bits 32-47 = total - 1, Bypass/Sequence Control Flag, Protocol Control Command Flag, OCF Flag, VCF Count Length), §4.1.4.2 (TFDF Header: rule 3 bits, UPID 5 bits, First Header or Last Valid Octet Pointer 16 bits for a fixed-length TFDZ), §4.1.4.1.8-9 (OID frames), §4.1.6 (FECF), §4.3.11.3.4 b and c (a frame of a Spacecraft ID, VCID, or MAP ID that is not valid is discarded), and Annex D1.3 (a truncated frame needs its VC's length, so it is not read without the VC). The inputs and configurations are those of the cases they replace (uslp-inv-005, -009, -010, uslp-oid-050, uslp-trunc-049, marked superseded by RS-023 / issue #232). A decode of a non-truncated frame of a Spacecraft ID, VCID, or MAP ID that the configuration does not hold reads it as its own fields say: the VCF Count Length and OCF Flag of the frame, no Security Header or Trailer; `validate_frame` rejects it. The truncated cases uslp-trunc-022, -023 keep UnknownChannel. Expected values read off the octets by the field widths above. The independent model of the other vector files of this codec (TV-023) does not cover this file: it was written before the change and is not touched by it; a blind-model round is the maintainer's decision (issue #232). Author: an AI agent, Claude Sonnet 5.5.",
